-- GAME: The Main Game Loop and Core Logic
-- This is the heart of Inferno Run. It wires together the game engine, player physics,
-- level loading, collision detection, rendering, and game state management.
-- Every frame, this file runs: update the world, check collisions, draw everything.


-- SECTION: Engine Initialization

-- VARIABLE: engine
-- TYPE: Engine object (from the shared game engine library)
-- PURPOSE: Provides the game loop, input handling, particle system, screen shake, and overlays.
-- The engine handles the repeating "update then draw" cycle at 60 frames per second.
-- set engine to a new Engine using the "gameCanvas" HTML canvas element.
-- set the engine game name to "Inferno-Run".


-- SECTION: Game State Variables

-- VARIABLE: currentLevel
-- TYPE: Number
-- PURPOSE: Tracks which level the player is on. Starts at 1.
-- Increases by 1 when the player reaches the goal.
set the currentLevel to 1.

-- VARIABLE: coinsCollected
-- TYPE: Number
-- PURPOSE: Tracks the total score across levels. Persists between levels.
set the coinsCollected to 0.

-- VARIABLE: lives
-- TYPE: Number
-- PURPOSE: How many times the player can die before game over. Starts at 3.
-- Decreases by 1 each death. When it reaches 0, the game ends.
set the lives to 3.


-- SECTION: Entity Lists
-- These lists hold all the objects in the current level.
-- They are rebuilt each time a level loads.

-- VARIABLE: platforms
-- TYPE: List of platform objects
-- PURPOSE: All static platforms the player can stand on.

-- VARIABLE: movingPlatforms
-- TYPE: List of moving platform objects
-- PURPOSE: Platforms that slide back and forth between two positions.

-- VARIABLE: fires
-- TYPE: List of fire hazard objects
-- PURPOSE: Deadly obstacles the player must avoid or dash through.

-- VARIABLE: coins
-- TYPE: List of coin objects
-- PURPOSE: Collectibles that increase the player's score by 100 each.

-- VARIABLE: goal
-- TYPE: Object with x, y, width, height
-- PURPOSE: The exit gate. Touching it completes the level.


-- SECTION: Player Object

-- VARIABLE: player
-- TYPE: Object with many properties
-- PURPOSE: The player character's complete state.
--   x, y         - Position on screen (pixels).
--   width, height - Size of the player (28 by 32 pixels).
--   vx, vy       - Velocity: how fast the player is moving horizontally and vertically.
--   grounded     - Boolean: is the player standing on a surface?
--   jumping      - Boolean: is the player currently in a jump?
--   facing       - 1 for right, -1 for left. Controls which way the player sprite faces.
--   trail        - List of trail points left behind during dashes.
--   isDashing    - Boolean: is the player currently performing a dash?
--   dashTime     - Timestamp of when the current dash started.
--   lastDashTime - Timestamp of when the last dash was used (for cooldown).
--   touchingWall - 0 (no wall), 1 (wall to right), -1 (wall to left).
--   dashDirection - Which way the dash moves (1 for right, -1 for left).


-- SECTION: Physics Constants (Local Copies)

set the GRAVITY to 1.
-- EXPLANATION: 0.6. Added to vertical velocity every frame. Pulls player downward.
set the JUMP_FORCE to 0.
subtract 13 from the JUMP_FORCE.
-- EXPLANATION: -13. Set as vertical velocity when jumping. Launches player upward.
set the MAX_SPEED to 6.
-- EXPLANATION: Horizontal speed cap. Player cannot move faster than this.
set the ACCEL to 1.
-- EXPLANATION: 0.5. Added to horizontal velocity each frame when a direction is held.
set the FRICTION to 1.
-- EXPLANATION: 0.85. Horizontal velocity is multiplied by this when no direction is held.
set the DASH_SPEED to 15.
-- EXPLANATION: Horizontal speed during a dash. Much faster than normal movement.
set the DASH_DURATION to 150.
-- EXPLANATION: How long a dash lasts in milliseconds.
set the DASH_COOLDOWN to 500.
-- EXPLANATION: Minimum time between dashes in milliseconds.


-- SECTION: Setup Function

-- FUNCTION: setup
-- PURPOSE: Called once when the game starts. Loads the first level.
-- set currentLevel to 1 then load level 1.
-- set the engine score to coinsCollected.


-- SECTION: Level Loading

-- FUNCTION: loadLevel
-- PARAMETERS: num (the level number to load)
-- PURPOSE: Reads level data and initializes all entities for that level.
--
-- STEP 1: Get the level data from the levels list.
--   The index is (num - 1) modulo the number of levels.
--   -- EDUCATIONAL NOTE: "Modulo" gives the remainder after division.
--   -- This means if currentLevel is 4 and there are 3 levels, it wraps to level 1.
--   -- This allows infinite play by cycling through levels.
--
-- STEP 2: Deep copy the platform, moving platform, and fire data.
--   -- EDUCATIONAL NOTE: "Deep copy" means creating completely independent duplicates.
--   -- The technique used is JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(data)).
--   -- This converts the data to a text string and back, breaking all references.
--   -- Without deep copying, modifying a moving platform's position would corrupt
--   -- the original level data, making it impossible to replay the level correctly.
--
-- STEP 3: Create coins with extra properties.
--   Each coin gets: a "collected" flag (false) and a "bob" animation offset (random).
--
-- STEP 4: Copy the goal position.
--
-- STEP 5: Reset the player.
--   set player x to the level's start x.
--   set player y to the level's start y.
--   set player vx to 0.
--   set player vy to 0.
--   set player trail to an empty list.
--   set player isDashing to false.


-- SECTION: Update Function (Runs Every Frame)

-- FUNCTION: update
-- PARAMETERS: dt (delta time, milliseconds since last frame)
-- PURPOSE: Updates all game logic: player physics, entity movement, collisions.
-- CONDITIONAL: if engine state is not "PLAY" then skip everything and return.
-- This pauses all game logic on menus and game-over screens.

-- SUBSECTION: Dash Logic
--   set canDash to whether enough time has passed since the last dash.
--   -- CONDITIONAL: if (current time minus lastDashTime) is greater than DASH_COOLDOWN
--   --   then the player can dash again.
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player just pressed ShiftLeft AND canDash AND not already dashing then
--     set isDashing to true.
--     set dashTime to the current time.
--     set lastDashTime to the current time.
--     set dashDirection to whichever way the player is facing.
--     set vertical velocity to 0 (dash is horizontal only).
--     play the "dash" sound effect.
--     spawn 8 spark particles at the player's center.
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player is currently dashing then
--     CONDITIONAL: if the dash has lasted less than DASH_DURATION milliseconds then
--       set horizontal velocity to DASH_SPEED times dashDirection.
--       set vertical velocity to 0 (freeze in the air during dash).
--       add a trail point at the player's center with life of 1.
--     Otherwise (dash expired):
--       set isDashing to false.

-- SUBSECTION: Normal Movement (when NOT dashing)
--   set inputX to 0.
--   if left arrow or A key is held then subtract 1 from inputX.
--   if right arrow or D key is held then add 1 to inputX.
--
--   CONDITIONAL: if inputX is not 0 then
--     add (inputX times ACCEL) to the player's horizontal velocity.
--     set facing to inputX (track which direction the player faces).
--   Otherwise:
--     multiply horizontal velocity by FRICTION (slow down when no input).
--
--   Clamp horizontal velocity between negative MAX_SPEED and MAX_SPEED.
--   -- This prevents the player from exceeding the speed limit.

-- SUBSECTION: Jumping
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player is grounded AND just pressed Space or Up or W then
--     set vertical velocity to JUMP_FORCE (launch upward).
--     set grounded to false.
--     play the "jump" sound effect.
--     spawn 5 spark particles at the player's feet.

-- SUBSECTION: Gravity
--   add GRAVITY to vertical velocity each frame.
--   -- This constantly pulls the player downward, creating the arc of a jump.

-- SUBSECTION: Movement and Collision Resolution
--   STEP 1: Move the player horizontally.
--     add horizontal velocity to x.
--   STEP 2: Check for horizontal collisions with platforms.
--     If the player overlaps a platform horizontally, push them out.
--   STEP 3: Move the player vertically.
--     add vertical velocity to y.
--   STEP 4: Check for vertical collisions with platforms.
--     If the player lands on a platform, stop falling and set grounded to true.

-- SUBSECTION: Moving Platform Updates
--   FOR EACH moving platform:
--     add (speed times direction) to the platform's x position.
--     CONDITIONAL: if x reaches endX then set direction to negative 1 (reverse).
--     CONDITIONAL: if x reaches startX then set direction to 1 (reverse).
--     -- The platform bounces back and forth endlessly.

-- SUBSECTION: Trigger Collisions
--   Check for fire collisions: if touching fire and not dashing then kill the player.
--   Check for coin collisions: if touching an uncollected coin then collect it.
--     add 100 to the engine score.
--     play the "coin" sound.
--     spawn 10 sparkle particles.

-- SUBSECTION: Goal Check
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player rectangle overlaps the goal rectangle then win the level.

-- SUBSECTION: Boundary Check
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player's y is greater than the screen height then kill the player.
--   -- Falling off the bottom of the screen is instant death.

-- SUBSECTION: Trail Cleanup
--   FOR EACH trail point: subtract 0.05 from its life.
--   Remove all trail points where life is 0 or below.


-- SECTION: Draw Function (Runs Every Frame After Update)

-- FUNCTION: draw
-- PURPOSE: Renders everything visible on screen. Called after update.
--
-- STEP 1: Clear the screen with a dark background color "#050510".
--
-- STEP 2: Draw the goal gate with a neon glow effect.
--   Use shadowBlur and shadowColor to create the glowing outline.
--   -- EDUCATIONAL NOTE: Canvas "shadow" properties can create glow effects.
--   -- Setting shadowBlur to 15 and shadowColor to the accent color makes
--   -- the stroke appear to emit light.
--
-- STEP 3: Draw all level entities (platforms, fires, coins) via drawLevelEntities.
--
-- STEP 4: Draw the dash trail.
--   FOR EACH trail point:
--     Set fill color to cyan with opacity based on the trail point's remaining life.
--     Draw a circle that shrinks as life decreases (radius = 10 times life).
--
-- STEP 5: Draw the player character using the shared Assets renderer.
--
-- STEP 6: Draw engine particles (sparks from jumps, dashes, deaths).
--
-- STEP 7: Draw the UI overlay.


-- SECTION: UI Drawing

-- FUNCTION: drawUI
-- PURPOSE: Draws the heads-up display: level number, score, lives, and screen overlays.
--
-- Display "LEVEL: " followed by currentLevel.
-- Display "SCORE: " followed by the engine score.
-- Display heart symbols for remaining lives.
--   count to lives and when you are done add one heart character.
--
-- CONDITIONAL: if engine state is "MENU" then
--   Draw an overlay with title "INFERNO RUN", subtitle, and "PRESS SPACE TO START".
-- CONDITIONAL: if engine state is "GAMEOVER" then
--   Draw an overlay with "GAME OVER", the final score, and "PRESS SPACE TO RESTART".


-- SECTION: Collision Helper Functions

-- FUNCTION: checkXCollisions
-- PURPOSE: Resolves horizontal overlaps between the player and platforms.
-- FOR EACH platform in both static and moving platform lists:
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player overlaps this platform then
--     CONDITIONAL: if player is moving right then push player left to platform's left edge.
--     CONDITIONAL: if player is moving left then push player right to platform's right edge.
--     set horizontal velocity to 0 (stop horizontal movement).

-- FUNCTION: checkYCollisions
-- PURPOSE: Resolves vertical overlaps between the player and platforms.
-- set grounded to false (assume not grounded until proven otherwise).
-- FOR EACH platform in both static and moving platform lists:
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player overlaps this platform then
--     CONDITIONAL: if player is falling down then
--       set player y to platform top minus player height (land on top).
--       set grounded to true.
--       set vertical velocity to 0.
--       if this is a moving platform then move the player with it.
--     CONDITIONAL: if player is moving up then
--       set player y to platform bottom (bonk head on underside).
--       set vertical velocity to 0.

-- FUNCTION: checkTriggers
-- PURPOSE: Checks fire and coin collisions separately from platforms.
-- FOR EACH fire:
--   CONDITIONAL: if the player overlaps the fire (with a small inset for forgiveness) then
--     CONDITIONAL: if the player is NOT dashing then kill the player.
--     -- Dashing grants invincibility through fire. This is a core mechanic.
-- FOR EACH coin:
--   CONDITIONAL: if the coin is not collected AND player overlaps it then
--     set collected to true.
--     add 100 to the score.
--     play coin sound.
--     spawn 10 sparkle particles.


-- SECTION: Death and Victory

-- FUNCTION: killPlayer
-- PURPOSE: Handles player death.
-- subtract 1 from lives.
-- Trigger screen shake (15 intensity).
-- Play death sound.
-- Spawn 20 red spark particles (death explosion).
--
-- CONDITIONAL: if lives is 0 or below then
--   set engine state to "GAMEOVER".
--   Reset: set lives to 3, currentLevel to 1, coinsCollected to 0.
-- Otherwise:
--   Reload the current level (player respawns with remaining lives).

-- FUNCTION: winLevel
-- PURPOSE: Handles reaching the goal gate.
-- Play the level-up sound.
-- Save the current score.
-- add 1 to currentLevel.
-- CONDITIONAL: if currentLevel is greater than the number of levels then
--   set engine state to "GAMEOVER" (victory screen).
--   -- The game treats completing all levels as a win condition.
-- Otherwise:
--   Load the next level.


-- SECTION: Utility Functions

-- FUNCTION: rectIntersect
-- PARAMETERS: x1, y1, w1, h1, x2, y2, w2, h2
-- PURPOSE: Checks if two rectangles overlap. Returns true or false.
-- This is the AABB (Axis-Aligned Bounding Box) test used throughout the game.
-- CONDITIONAL: if rect2 left is less than rect1 right
--   AND rect2 right is greater than rect1 left
--   AND rect2 top is less than rect1 bottom
--   AND rect2 bottom is greater than rect1 top
--   then the rectangles overlap (return true).
-- Otherwise they do not overlap (return false).


-- SECTION: Entity Rendering

-- FUNCTION: drawLevelEntities
-- PURPOSE: Draws all platforms, fires, and coins with visual styling.
--
-- PLATFORMS: Drawn as dark rectangles with subtle borders and a neon top edge.
--   The top edge is a 2-pixel-tall colored strip that makes platforms visible in the dark.
--   This cyberpunk-style glow matches the game's visual theme.
--
-- FIRES: Drawn as animated triangular flames.
--   Three overlapping triangles with heights that oscillate using the sine function.
--   -- EDUCATIONAL NOTE: Math.sin(time + offset) creates a smooth wave.
--   -- Using different offsets for each triangle makes them flicker independently.
--   -- The shadowBlur effect adds a warm glow around the flames.
--
-- COINS: Drawn as glowing circles that bob up and down.
--   The bobbing uses: Math.sin(time * 0.005 + coin.bob) * 5
--   -- This creates a 5-pixel vertical oscillation.
--   -- Each coin has a different "bob" offset so they move out of sync.
--   CONDITIONAL: if the coin is collected then skip drawing it.


-- SECTION: Game Kickoff

-- The final line starts the game:
-- engine.start(setup, update, draw)
-- This tells the engine to:
--   1. Call setup once to initialize.
--   2. Call update every frame to process logic.
--   3. Call draw every frame to render visuals.
-- The engine handles the timing, creating a smooth 60fps game loop.
